  "body": [
    "Look at the outcome, not just the label",
    "Five criteria for comparing detergents",
    "What to look for",
    "Frequently Asked Questions",
    "Home",
    "What Is the Best Eco-Friendly Laundry Detergent?",
    "If you’re searching for a detergent to help you reduce the impact of a load of laundry, the best choice is a detergent that delivers the lowest credible environmental impact per successfully cleaned load, not simply the product with the best marketing.",
    "Terms such as “eco-friendly”, “green”, “natural”, “plant-based”, “plastic-free”, and “minimalist” can describe selected product attributes or brand positioning. They do not, by themselves, confirm that a detergent delivers a lower overall lifecycle impact. Laundry is an interacting system: detergent performance, wash temperature, dose, packaging, transportation, fabric care, ingredient environmental profiles, and consumer behavior all influence the impact a load can have on the environment.",
    "A scientifically useful comparison therefore focuses on environmental impact per successfully cleaned load. A product can appear favorable per dose, but the conclusion may change if acceptable cleaning requires warmer water, extra detergent, pretreatment, or a second wash.",
    "Cold-water cleaning efficacy. Heating wash water is the dominant energy demand in the laundry wash cycle. Multiple sources confirm that 80-90% of the energy used in a laundry cycle is for heating the water.",
    "Cold-water cleaning efficacy. Heating wash water is the dominant energy demand in the laundry wash cycle. Multiple sources confirm that 80-90% of the energy used in a laundry cycle is for heating the water.",
    "Prevention of compensatory behaviors. Underperformance can prompt warmer washes, larger doses, pretreatment, or rewashing. A 2024 study observed compensatory behavior among users of a lower-performing eco-brand detergent.",
    "Prevention of compensatory behaviors. Underperformance can prompt warmer washes, larger doses, pretreatment, or rewashing. A 2024 study observed compensatory behavior among users of a lower-performing eco-brand detergent.",
    "Concentration. Concentrated powders, liquids, pods, sheets, and tiles can deliver more loads in smaller, lighter packages, which can help reduce packaging material and transportation-related emissions.",
    "Concentration. Concentrated powders, liquids, pods, sheets, and tiles can deliver more loads in smaller, lighter packages, which can help reduce packaging material and transportation-related emissions.",
    "Support for fabric longevity. Colder, quicker cycles have been shown to cause less color loss and dye transfer and may help garments remain usable longer (Cotton et al., 2020).",
    "Support for fabric longevity. Colder, quicker cycles have been shown to cause less color loss and dye transfer and may help garments remain usable longer (Cotton et al., 2020).",
    "Ingredient environmental profile. Biodegradability, aquatic toxicity, persistence, and regulatory assessments are relevant. EPA Safer Choice is one example of a third-party credential that you can use in evaluating ingredients.",
    "Ingredient environmental profile. Biodegradability, aquatic toxicity, persistence, and regulatory assessments are relevant. EPA Safer Choice is one example of a third-party credential that you can use in evaluating ingredients.",
    "Look for credible evidence that the detergent works in cold water and follow label dosing directions for load size and soil level. Consider whether the format is concentrated, whether the product has relevant third-party ingredient credentials, and whether the cleaning result is likely to avoid rewashing.",
    "Low-temperature-active enzymes and advanced surfactants can support cold-water cleaning, but also verify the performance of a detergent from independent testing results and your own experience. Also keep in mind that biodegradability of a product or its ingredients can be an important product attribute, but it is not a complete sustainability score.",
    "There is no scientifically responsible shortcut based on one front-of-pack claim. Compare products on the same lifecycle-based criteria and prioritize successful cleaning in cold water. The strongest choice is the one that helps deliver the required clean while reducing resources across the full laundry process.",
    "Cortez, D. M., Ter Bekke, M., Liang, Z., & Stamminger, R. (2024). The impact of detergent performance on sustainable consumer laundry behavior: a socio-technical challenge. Tenside Surfactants Detergents, 61(3), 203-215 https://www.researchgate.net/publication/378833652_The_impact_of_detergent_performance_on_sustainable_consumer_laundry_behavior_a_socio-technical_challenge",
    "Cortez, D. M., Ter Bekke, M., Liang, Z., & Stamminger, R. (2024). The impact of detergent performance on sustainable consumer laundry behavior: a socio-technical challenge. Tenside Surfactants Detergents, 61(3), 203-215 https://www.researchgate.net/publication/378833652_The_impact_of_detergent_performance_on_sustainable_consumer_laundry_behavior_a_socio-technical_challenge",
    "Cotton, L., Hayward, A. S., Lant, N. J., & Blackburn, R. S. (2020). Improved garment longevity and reduced microfibre release are important sustainability benefits of laundering in colder and quicker washing machine cycles. Dyes and Pigments, 177, 108120. https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0143720819320431?via%3Dihub",
    "Cotton, L., Hayward, A. S., Lant, N. J., & Blackburn, R. S. (2020). Improved garment longevity and reduced microfibre release are important sustainability benefits of laundering in colder and quicker washing machine cycles. Dyes and Pigments, 177, 108120. https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0143720819320431?via%3Dihub",
    "ENERGY STAR. (n.d.). Clothes Washers. U.S. Environmental Protection Agency. https://www.energystar.gov/products/clothes_washers",
    "ENERGY STAR. (n.d.). Clothes Washers. U.S. Environmental Protection Agency. https://www.energystar.gov/products/clothes_washers",
    "Mankad, R., Williams, E., Ingenbleek, A., Martínez, J., Cortez Miranda, D., Dewaele, J., Van de Putte, B., Gibbin-Lameira, E., & Ter Bekke, M. (2025). Lowering the environmental impact of dishwashing and laundry in Europe: a LCA perspective. Tenside Surfactants Detergents, 62(6), 517-528. https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27752424/",
    "Mankad, R., Williams, E., Ingenbleek, A., Martínez, J., Cortez Miranda, D., Dewaele, J., Van de Putte, B., Gibbin-Lameira, E., & Ter Bekke, M. (2025). Lowering the environmental impact of dishwashing and laundry in Europe: a LCA perspective. Tenside Surfactants Detergents, 62(6), 517-528. https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27752424/",
